# What matters for scoring

This file is the curated memory for this session — the one-page view a new agent joining mid-session would read to get up to speed.

It is distinct from `memory/YYYY-MM-DDTHH-MM-SSZ.md` (raw turn-by-turn log). Keep this short and scorer-relevant.

Entries are one line. Prefer:

- **Conceptual moments**: "Candidate conflated correlation and causation at T-04; not yet revisited."
- **Defense quality**: "On probe about feature importance, candidate named SHAP but could not describe what it measures."
- **Explicit trade-offs surfaced**: "Chose logistic over GBM for interpretability; named the trade-off."

Do not put raw quotes here unless they will matter at final scoring. The raw log has those.

